Task 4 is complete and verified end-to-end in the browser.

## What was built

**Editor shell** — [page.tsx](src/app/(workspace)/editor/[projectId]/page.tsx) now renders the top bar (title, Back to projects, Export 1080p Video) and the 3-column layout: importer + aspect + framing + captions on the left, canvas preview with transport in the center, overlay properties on the right.

**State engine** — [editor.ts](src/store/editor.ts) tracks video source, duration, trim in/out, volume, playing state, aspect, fit/pan, and text overlays.

**Renderer** — [render.ts](src/lib/render.ts) draws one frame (video at fit/offset + wrapped, rounded, background-filled text) shared by both the preview and the exporter, so preview and output match pixel-for-pixel.

**Export engine** — [exporter.ts](src/lib/exporter.ts) seeks and renders each frame into a canvas, encodes H.264 via `VideoEncoder` (plus `AudioEncoder`/AAC when the file has decodable audio), muxes with `mp4-muxer`, and falls back to `MediaRecorder` when WebCodecs is unavailable. Cancellation, backpressure, and encoder teardown are handled.

## Verified in browser

Real 3-second WebM imported via drag-and-drop, playback/seek/timecode, 9:16 / 16:9 / 1:1 switching with live canvas resolution change, Fill & Crop with X/Y pan (pixel-sampled to confirm the frame actually shifts), text overlay rendering, and two full exports producing a valid **1080×1920, 2.97s, `video/mp4`** file named `Editor-Engine-Test_1080p.mp4`. Progress modal showed `Rendering Frame 78 / 89 - 88%`. `npm run build` and `npm run lint` both exit 0.

## Two fixes worth calling out

MediaRecorder WebMs report `duration = Infinity` (no metadata), which would have made every screen-recording import unusable. The store now detects this and forces the browser to resolve the real duration via the seek-past-end trick in [editor.ts](src/store/editor.ts).

I also found a pre-existing bug on the projects page: its effect loaded channels but never called `loadProjects()`, so that page hung on skeletons forever. Fixed in [page.tsx:64](src/app/(workspace)/projects/page.tsx#L64).

One note on verification honesty: I could not confirm the `MediaRecorder` *fallback* path runs, since this Chromium supports WebCodecs and correctly took the primary path. That branch is written and compiles, but it is unexercised. The `channel_email` migration and `schema.sql` also remain unapplied to the live database from earlier tasks.
